        "execSummary":  "The Nemotron-LangChain result challenges the assumption that better agents require bigger or more expensive models ΓÇö harness engineering (prompt tuning, tool design, middleware optimization) can close most of the performance gap against closed frontier models at a fraction of the cost. For enterprise AI platform leaders, the open-stack architecture gives full customization and control over the agent environment, a significant governance advantage over black-box API-only models. The 90% cost reduction claim merits independent validation, but even at half that savings, open-model agentic stacks become economically competitive for high-volume enterprise deployments. EY and Box as early adopters signal that professional services and knowledge-work verticals are actively evaluating open-model agent stacks today.",
